.TH XNVME-DRIVER-ATTACH 1 "15 October 2026" "xNVMe" "xNVMe"
.SH NAME
\fBxnvme-driver-attach \fP- Attach the userspace driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.fam C
\fBxnvme\fP \fIdriver-attach\fP <bdf>\.\.\. [\fB--driver\fP <name>] [\fB--force\fP] [\fB--all\fP]
                    [\fB--dry-run\fP]
.fam T
.fi
.fam T
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Move each named NVMe controller function off the kernel nvme driver, onto the platform's userspace driver unless \fB--driver\fP names another: on Linux vfio-pci when the host has IOMMU groups or vfio no-IOMMU mode, else uio_pci_generic, and nic_uio on FreeBSD. A function whose namespaces are in use is refused; \fB--force\fP overrides only the refusal of a namespace carrying a filesystem or partition table. \fB--all\fP attaches every function on the kernel nvme driver, and skips those in use.
.RE
.PP


